  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock id="HHEBA1CD44839C108D1DAFD6DE3427BE45" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="HH22FBAEA0509E80B804A4341B1670898A" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;9. On July 18, 2018, in Docket No. PL17-1-001, the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("Commission") dismissed the requests for rehearing and clarification of its revised policy statement on treatment of income taxes (&amp;#8220;Revised Policy Statement&amp;#8221;) and provided guidance regarding the treatment of accumulated deferred income taxes ("ADIT") in light of its revised policy. Inquiry Regarding the Commissions Policy for Recovery of Income Tax Costs, Order on Rehearing of Revised Policy Statement, 164 FERC &amp;#182; 61,030 (Jul 18, 2018) (&amp;#8221;July 18 Order&amp;#8221;). Pursuant to the guidance provided by the Commission in its July 18 Order, Texas Eastern Transmission, LP (&amp;#8220;Texas Eastern&amp;#8221;), an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of (a tax pass-through entity owned in part by) Spectra Energy Partners, LP (&amp;#8220;SEP&amp;#8221;), a master limited partnership, intends to remove any balances recorded in Accounts 190, 281, 282, and 283 of the Commission&amp;#8217;s Uniform System of Accounts, as well as excess ADIT that has been transferred to Account 254 and deficient ADIT that has been transferred to Account 182.3. Texas Eastern has requested approval in Docket No. AC18-220 from the Chief Accountant of the Commission to implement the accounting entries necessary for removing these balances. The request is currently pending. Upon receipt of the Chief Accountant&amp;#8217;s approval, Texas Eastern will reflect the removal of these balances in the annual and quarterly financing reporting required by Part 260 of the Commission&amp;#8217;s regulations. On November 27, 2023, SEP, a subsidiary of Enbridge Inc., filed with the Commission in Docket No. AC18-220-000 a request on behalf of certain of SEP&amp;#8217;s pipeline and affiliates, including Texas Eastern, for a Motion for Action on its September 10, 2018, request for approval of accounting entries in this proceeding.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock id="HH582A4E700260C05D782FA2D6F218758A" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedIncreaseOrDecreaseInAnnualRevenuesCausedByImportantRateChangesTextBlock id="HHE60759687E403C6B3DE58B8464A791E0" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;11. On June 3, 2024, Texas Eastern filed its petition for approval of the Stipulation and Agreement (&amp;#8220;2024 Settlement&amp;#8221;) related to the May 3, 2024, prepackaged 2024 settlement, and on July 31, 2024, Texas Eastern received approval from the FERC of its uncontested rate settlement (&amp;#8220;July 2024 Order&amp;#8221;).&amp;#160; Pursuant to the July 2024 Order and the 2024 Settlement, Texas Eastern is required to file two actual tariff records reflecting rate effective dates of October 1, 2024, and January 1, 2026.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;Pursuant to the July 2024 Order and terms of the 2024 Settlement, on September 3, 2024 and November 7, 2025, Texas Eastern filed actual tariff records reflecting rate effective dates of October 1, 2024 and January 1, 2026, respectively. Texas Eastern will continue to operate under those rates effective January 1, 2026.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedIncreaseOrDecreaseInAnnualRevenuesCausedByImportantRateChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock id="HHC9E9219375AC2F82A8CDFAF00D88FECC" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;12. Uses the officers of its General Partner, Spectra Energy Transmission Services, LLC:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;Removals, effective 01/23/2026&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;Capps, Allen C., President&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;Huffman, Robert L., Vice President, U.S. Operations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;Tessin, Caitlin L., VP, Market Innovation and Gulf Coast Business Development&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;Wolfe, Jeffrey J., Vice President, Business Development Southeast&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;Removal, effective 02/01/2026&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;Moeller III, Edward F., Vice President, Business Development &amp;amp; Marketing, Louisiana and Offshore&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;Appointments, effective 01/23/2026&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;Goff, Diana D., Vice President, U.S. Operations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;Huffman, Robert L., President&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;Knight-Turcan, Kurt,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;Tessin, Caitilin L., Vice President, Commercial Gas Transmission and Midstream&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;Appointment, effective 02/01/2026&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0in;"&gt;Khan, Zeyd, Vice President, Business Development &amp;amp; Marketing, Louisiana and Offshore&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock id="HHD790CCB2EDB33AB49E3957CEAFD4E7D7" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; margin-bottom: 0in; text-align: center; line-height: normal;" align="center"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;NOTES TO FINANCIAL STATEMENTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; margin-bottom: 0in; text-align: center; line-height: normal;" align="center"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;For the Three Months Ended March 31, 2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; margin-bottom: 0in; text-align: center; line-height: normal;" align="center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;These interim financial statements should be read in conjunction with the financial statements and notes thereto contained in the Form 2 of Texas Eastern Transmission, LP (TETLP), for the year ended December 31, 2025. These financial statements are unaudited, but in management&amp;#8217;s opinion, reflect all normal recurring adjustments that are necessary for a fair presentation of financial position, results of operations and cash flows for the period presented. The results as presented for this interim period are not necessarily indicative of results to be achieved for the full year. Certain information and notes which would substantially duplicate the disclosures contained in the most recent FERC Form 2 have been omitted.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HH26F298D96F05ADD051F0C74B218AC0A3" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4"></ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
