              <td class="xl285">165,295</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="mso-height-source: userset; height: 15.0pt;">
              <td class="xl283" style="height: 15.0pt;" height="20">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160; Total</td>
              <td class="xl284">284,116</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="HH619F68CC642ADE5177C1660EF32AC89A" xlink:to="HH080E64FBCB2B94CC9038B9CC2ED109B9" order="1" />
    <link:loc xlink:type="locator" xlink:href="#HH0A4335631B6DBE94A8619F6FA50E02BE" xlink:label="HH0A4335631B6DBE94A8619F6FA50E02BE" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="HH0FAD32A8BFC007781CD6E5BD7761BC88" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <table style="width: 464pt;" border="0" width="619" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
          <tbody>
            <tr style="mso-height-source: userset; height: 15.0pt;">
              <td class="xl283" style="height: 15.0pt; width: 464pt;" width="619" height="20">Since we administer the recovery of gas used for fuel by means of a tracking mechanism with a&#160;</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="mso-height-source: userset; height: 15.0pt;">
              <td class="xl283" style="height: 15.0pt;" height="20">cash transaction-based make-up provision, no dollar values are assigned to the net excesses or&#160;</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="mso-height-source: userset; height: 15.0pt;">
              <td class="xl283" style="height: 15.0pt;" height="20">deficiencies which results from shipper supplied gas.&#160; The dollar values reported are for the sole&#160;</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="mso-height-source: userset; height: 15.0pt;">
              <td class="xl283" style="height: 15.0pt;" height="20">purpose of complying with this schedule.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="HH0A4335631B6DBE94A8619F6FA50E02BE" xlink:to="HH0FAD32A8BFC007781CD6E5BD7761BC88" order="1" />
    <link:loc xlink:type="locator" xlink:href="#HH59E873B54169904D94E09F97F0EDA7A4" xlink:label="HH59E873B54169904D94E09F97F0EDA7A4" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="HH2BD2776FCB8817308E34149D65ECA6EC" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <table style="width: 464pt;" border="0" width="619" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
          <tbody>
            <tr style="mso-height-source: userset; height: 15.0pt;">
              <td class="xl283" style="height: 15.0pt; width: 464pt;" width="619" height="20">Fuel quantities requiring an allocation are assigned to the rate categories on the basis of the&#160;</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="mso-height-source: userset; height: 15.0pt;">
              <td class="xl283" style="height: 15.0pt;" height="20">stated fuel rates as referenced in Order No. 710-C, at paragraph 9.&#160; Specifically, within each&#160;</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="mso-height-source: userset; height: 15.0pt;">
              <td class="xl283" style="height: 15.0pt;" height="20">functional category, the fuel quantities in lines 8 &#8211; 30 are prorated to the rate categories based on&#160;</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="mso-height-source: userset; height: 15.0pt;">
              <td class="xl283" style="height: 15.0pt;" height="20">the ratio of the Shipper Supplied quantities in lines 1 - 7 for each rate category to the total&#160;</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="mso-height-source: userset; height: 15.0pt;">
              <td class="xl283" style="height: 15.0pt;" height="20">Shipper Supplied quantity for such functional category.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="mso-height-source: userset; height: 15.0pt;">
              <td class="xl283" style="height: 15.0pt;" height="20">&#160;</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="mso-height-source: userset; height: 15.0pt;">
              <td class="xl283" style="height: 15.0pt;" height="20">Disposition of Excess Gas and Gas Acquired to Meet Deficiency quantities in lines 38 &#8211; 65 are&#160;</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="mso-height-source: userset; height: 15.0pt;">
              <td class="xl283" style="height: 15.0pt;" height="20">prorated to the rate categories based on the ratio of the Excess or Deficiency quantities for each&#160;</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="mso-height-source: userset; height: 15.0pt;">
              <td class="xl283" style="height: 15.0pt;" height="20">rate category to the total Excess or Deficiency quantity in line 37.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="HH59E873B54169904D94E09F97F0EDA7A4" xlink:to="HH2BD2776FCB8817308E34149D65ECA6EC" order="1" />
